  "title": "merge: squelch some compiler warnings.",
  "description": "The number of files to be processed by merge_files_common() should never\nbe zero, so the loop over all files should be executed at least once.\n\nmerge_open_in_files() is called for each file; if it returns 0, it sets\nerr_fileno, so that shouldn't result in err_fileno being used when not\nset.\n\nmerge_process_packets() is also called, and if it returns anything other\nthan MERGE_OK, it will set err, err_info, err_fileno, and err_framenum,\nso it's not clear why, on Linux Mint, the compiler thinks err_framenum\nis being used without being set.\n\nPerhaps the assertion test for in_file_count > 0 isn't being done\nbecause NDEBUG is set, and it thinks you might never execute the loop;\nhowever, in that case, status, which is initialized to MERGE_OK, will\nstill be MERGE_OK, so the error-reporting code should never be executed.\n\nFor now, we just initialize err, err_fileno, and err_framenum to 0 and\nerr_info to NULL, given that we're already initializing status to\nMERGE_OK.\n\nWhile we're at it, remove some unnecessary settings of err_framenum.",
